course: dictionary
lesson: 11221
title: The woodlouse is not an insect
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A woodlouse is a small grey animal with a hard, jointed shell and fourteen legs. You can spot one by its legs and its shell, not by its name. «A spider has eight legs and is not an insect, a woodlouse has fourteen legs, and centipedes and millipedes have many more, so counting legs is the quickest way to tell them apart.» The sentence gives the clue: count the legs.
explain: Many people call a woodlouse a bug, but scientists are careful with that word. «Sam told his little cousin that eating a bug would give him a superpower; the cousin ate a woodlouse and cried, and his aunt was raging.» The cousin cried and the aunt was raging, so Sam's story was a trick. A woodlouse gives you no superpower, and it is not an insect either.
explain: Look at the other clues in the sentences. «A woodlouse has 14 legs and is a crustacean, related to crabs.» Crustacean is the hard word here. Crabs have a hard shell too, so a crustacean is a shelled animal with jointed legs, and the woodlouse is its relative. Insects have six legs and three body parts, so the woodlouse does not fit that group.
fact: A woodlouse is a small grey animal with a hard, jointed shell and fourteen legs.
fact: Woodlice live in damp, dark places such as under stones, logs and leaves.
fact: Woodlice are crustaceans, related to crabs, so they are not insects.
fact: Some kinds roll up into a ball when in danger, and they are called pill bugs.
fact: Woodlice are decomposers: they eat dead leaves and wood, which helps recycle nutrients.
exercise: «A woodlouse has 14 legs and is a crustacean, related to crabs.» How many legs does a woodlouse have? | *fourteen | six | ten | eight
exercise: «Some kinds can roll up into a ball when in danger.» What is another name for these kinds? | *pill bug | centipede | spider
exercise: Where does a woodlouse like to live? | On the tops of tall trees in the sun | Hot, dry deserts | *Damp, dark places like under stones and logs
test: «A woodlouse is related to crabs.» Which animal is also a crustacean? | snail | spider | *crab | ladybird
test: «Centipedes and millipedes have many more legs.» Which animal has the most legs? | spider | woodlouse | *millipede | insect
exam: «Sam told his little cousin that eating a bug would give him a superpower; the cousin ate a woodlouse and cried, and his aunt was raging.» Why was the aunt raging? | The woodlouse gave the cousin a superpower | *Sam tricked his little cousin into eating a woodlouse with a false promise | The cousin ate a spider with eight legs | Sam won a prize at school
